            <h2>Culture and Coastal Atmosphere</h2>

            <p>This is a part of Key West known for its artistic spirit and maritime heritage. Street entertainers convene at Mallory Square each evening to party as the sun sets, with music and entertainment. There are colourful works inspired by ocean life and tropical landscapes on view at local art galleries. </p>

            <p>The cruise to Key West takes you through this culture in a day without feeling dragged or snowed. The small size of the island practically invites you to wander along side streets and waterfront paths. This combination of history, artistic creativity and coastal landscape gives it an unmistakable atmosphere. </p>

            <h2>That was life onboard during a cruise to Key West. </h2>

            <p>Onboard, life during a cruise to Key West is casual and tropical. Destination-focused, it offers open decks, ocean breezes and island-themed entertainment. As anticipation builds, guests invariably gather to watch the Florida coastline come in. </p>

            <p>Evenings on board, after leaving Key West behind, have an easygoing atmosphere shaped by the island's allure. Whether on a Royal Caribbean cruise to Key West or any other line, the experience is consistent from port call to sea day. </p>

